    "batch-community-final-438-q040": {"answers":["A"],"confidence":"preference","basis":"concept","explanation":"BMI 37 indicates obesity. Excess body fat raises breast cancer risk particularly after menopause, making breast carcinoma the best of the listed choices. Age 38 alone does not establish menopausal status, and the HbA1c cannot estimate this patient's cancer risk.","references":[{"title":"National Cancer Institute · Obesity and cancer","url":"https://www.cancer.gov/about-cancer/causes-prevention/risk/obesity/obesity-fact-sheet"}]},
    "batch-community-final-438-q057": {"answers":["C"],"confidence":"supported","basis":"lecture","explanation":"At age 48, a screening mammogram is appropriate. One second-degree relative with breast cancer may warrant a family-history assessment, but the stem supplies no high-risk mutation or risk estimate that would justify MRI as the initial screening test.","references":[{"title":"USPSTF · Breast cancer screening","url":"https://www.uspreventiveservicestaskforce.org/uspstf/recommendation/breast-cancer-screening"}],"evidence":{"title":"CMED 311 Cancer Lecture 2026","cohortLabel":"MED444","url":"https://drive.google.com/file/d/138I0BdP44o8tE9Uo56sdEQ1h2irdVe4t/view#page=29","unit":"page","page":29,"quote":"The USPSTF recommends biennial screening mammography for women aged 40 to 74 years.","relation":"direct","image":"lecture-media/community-batch-review/138I0BdP44o8tE9Uo56sdEQ1h2irdVe4t-029.jpg","sourceSha256":"eae4cf202d2f44847ccdda47b9e005f2ef0f3f34ea453d6ed25a3c10181ba699","imageSha256":"9d6b6ffab1df7290f7b15b861c32ae9a019f511fe848053ec8b63713766163fc"}},
    "batch-community-final-437-q004": {"answers":["A"],"confidence":"supported","basis":"concept","explanation":"This asks about new cases, rather than deaths. In the IARC 2024 global estimates, lung cancer was the most frequently diagnosed cancer in men. Rankings can differ by year and region.","references":[{"title":"IARC · GLOBOCAN 2024 worldwide cancer estimates","url":"https://gco.iarc.who.int/media/globocan/factsheets/populations/900-world-fact-sheet.pdf"}]},
